# Build context exclusions.
#
# Without this file, `COPY . .` baked the live IG and Telegram credentials
# into an image layer (/app/.env, 440 bytes), plus a build-time snapshot of
# the trade journal and candle archive (15M) and the log directory (9.1M).
# The data/ and logs/ volume mounts shadow those at runtime, which is exactly
# why nobody noticed: everything worked, and the credentials survived in a
# layer regardless of anything done to .env afterwards.
#
# WHAT MUST NOT BE ADDED HERE
# ---------------------------
# scripts/ — a weekly VPS cron runs it FROM INSIDE the container:
#   0 9 * * 1 docker exec ig-trading-bot python3 /app/scripts/tick_entry_readout.py
# Excluding it would break that readout silently, into /root/tick-readout.log.
#
# tests/ is deliberately KEPT (164KB) so the golden suite can be run against
# the container itself:
#   docker exec ig-trading-bot python3 -m unittest discover -s tests -t .
# which is the most direct proof that live computes the validated numbers.

# Credentials
.env
.env.*

# Runtime state — both are bind-mounted volumes; the image copy is dead weight
# that is shadowed the moment the container starts.
data/
logs/

# Virtual environments (~310MB of build context)
venv/
.venv/
.venv-bt/
*.old

# VCS and tooling
.git/
.github/
.claude/
.gitignore
.dockerignore

# Python artefacts
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# Local-only
CLAUDE.local.md
backtest_results/
.DS_Store
